			"notes": {
				"rationale": "The conventional support-verb expression is non-idiomatic but lexically restricted: treffen only supports Entscheidung, a Collocation (de/funktionsverbgefuege-are-collocations), whose members are the verb, the noun and its own article eine. Its contextual Surface follows sentence order and takes the finite verb's features. Knowledge (#884): Nom S · (über + Acc T), the frame taking on the noun's government as one predicate, entscheiden über (user ruling R4, 2026-10-03). entscheiden is a synonym on Duden's explicit Synonyme listing under entscheiden, not on the gloss (etwas entscheiden) under Entscheidung (R3); eine Entscheidung fällen is a synonym and einen Entschluss fassen a near-synonym from the OpenThesaurus synset. Decided by agents under the user's delegation. sich entscheiden is a near-synonym too, since it fits only choosing and takes no über; einen Beschluss treffen, sich entschließen and eine Wahl treffen are dropped (user, 2026-10-03, on the judges' split)."
			},
